Local patch for Pi-Somfy Release 3.3 (01d19f2): stop treating every Pi as a Pi 5.

Pi-Somfy reads /proc/device-tree/model, and then *also* guesses "Pi 5" whenever
/dev/gpiochip4 exists. Current Raspberry Pi OS kernels create gpiochip4 -> gpiochip0
on every Pi, so a Pi 3 or 4 on Trixie ends up on the experimental lgpio path, with
software-timed RTS frames, instead of pigpio's DMA timing. This limits the guess to
when the model file cannot be read (the Docker case the upstream comment describes).

Apply:   cd /opt/Pi-Somfy && sudo git apply /opt/somfy-shutters/deploy/pi-somfy-pi5-detection.patch
Check:   grep -E "pigpio|lgpio" /var/log/operateShutters.log | tail -2
         -> "pigpio's pi instantiated", not "lgpio ... (Pi 5)"

diff --git a/operateShutters.py b/operateShutters.py
index 5c4b257..feac5a6 100755
--- a/operateShutters.py
+++ b/operateShutters.py
@@ -62,16 +62,20 @@ import socket
 # fall back to checking for /dev/gpiochip4 (RP1 chip, Pi 5 only) or the
 # CPU revision code in /proc/cpuinfo.
 IS_PI5 = False
+_MODEL_READ = False
 LGPIO_CHIP = 4   # gpiochip number for lgpio (Pi 5): 4 on older kernels, 0 on newer
 if not WINDOWS:
     try:
         with open('/proc/device-tree/model', 'r') as f:
             _model = f.read()
+        _MODEL_READ = True  # local patch: model known, skip the gpiochip4 guess
         if 'Pi 5' in _model:
             IS_PI5 = True
     except (FileNotFoundError, PermissionError):
         pass
-    if not IS_PI5 and os.path.exists('/dev/gpiochip4'):
+    # local patch: every Pi on current kernels has a gpiochip4 -> gpiochip0 link, so this
+    # guess is only safe when the model file could not be read (Docker, per the note above).
+    if not IS_PI5 and not _MODEL_READ and os.path.exists('/dev/gpiochip4'):
         IS_PI5 = True
     if not IS_PI5:
         try:
